<!--
  Device administration policies SecureChat asks for.

  Only what is actually used is listed. Every extra policy widens what a bug in this app is capable
  of doing to somebody's handset, and unused policies are pure downside: they cost the operator
  trust at the provisioning prompt and buy nothing.

  wipe-data  - remote destruction of a lost or seized handset, gated by DeviceWipeAuthority.
  force-lock - lock the screen on demand; a proportionate response short of destroying data.

  Managed configuration (setApplicationRestrictions) needs no entry here: it comes from device
  owner, not from a device-admin policy.
-->
<device-admin xmlns:android="http://schemas.android.com/apk/res/android">
    <uses-policies>
        <wipe-data />
        <force-lock />
    </uses-policies>
</device-admin>
